__**Concept:**__



Surface Area (Sphere): 4pi r²

Surface Area (Cube): 6a²

Volume (Sphere): (4)/(3)pi r³

Volume (Cube): a³

__**Calculation:**__

Given surface areas equal: 4pi r²=6a²

r and a are radii and side respectively.

Find r/a

⇒ r²=(3)/(2pi)a²

⇒ (r)/(a)=sqrt{(3)/(2pi)}

Volume ratio

⇒ dfrac{V_s}{V_c}=dfrac{(4)/(3)pi r³}{a³}

⇒ dfrac{V_s}{V_c}=(4)/(3)pi((r)/(a))³

⇒ dfrac{V_s}{V_c}=(4)/(3)pi((3)/(2pi))³/² = ((3)/(2pi))³/² =frac{3³/²}{2³/²pi³/²}

⇒ (4)/(3)pi· frac{3³/²}{2³/²pi³/²} =(4)/(3)·frac{3³/²}{2³/²}·pi¹⁻³/²

⇒ (4)/(3)· frac{3sqrt{3}}{2sqrt{2}}·pi⁻¹/²

⇒ 4·frac{sqrt{3}}{2sqrt{2}} times(1)/(sqrt{pi)}

⇒ 2·sqrt{(3)/(2)} times(1)/(sqrt{pi)}

⇒ sqrt{4}·sqrt{(3)/(2)} times(1)/(sqrt{pi)}

⇒ frac{sqrt{6}}{sqrt{pi}}

**∴ Ratio of volumes = sqrt{6}:sqrt{pi}**
